# Distribution weight calculations, Chemist1975
# Source: https://publications.gc.ca/collections/Collection-R/Statcan/63-210-XIB/0009863-210-XIB.pdf
# Statistics Canada, Retail Industry, 1998
# This gives floor areas of various types of shop which can be used to construct relative distribution weights.
# Reference value: ClothingShop1990 at 100 distributionweight (clothes stores are by far an extremely common retailer)
# Total floor area of Canadian clothing stores, 1998: 2,977,703 m2
# Total floor area of Canadian pharmacies (aka chemists), 1998: 463,960 m2
# 463960 / 2977703 = 0.155 * 100 = ~16
#
# For Chemist1955, we will use c. 1978 figures as they are also what ClothesShop1960 are derived from
# 1978 drug store floor area: 2,157,698 ft2
# 1978 clothes store floor area: 10,188,827 ft2
# Ratio: 2157698/10188827 = 0.211 * 40 distweight for ClothesShop1960 = 8.47 ~ 8
#
# TODO: Possibly slot in a Chemist1920 or so to cover the large gap between Chemist1860 and Chemist1955, and use c. 1930 Canadian numbers to estimate store count.

